  "name_en": "Noyon Cathedral",
  "summary": "Rebuilt after a fire in 1131, Noyon is one of the earliest Gothic cathedrals, with a four-storey elevation of arcade, gallery, triforium and clerestory and a rounded transept. Work ran from the 1140s to the early 13th century. It was badly hit in the First World War and rebuilt between 1918 and 1938.",
